generated_hash =

// @vibe/compiler/cache — ADR-0070 / #897 compiler-internal contract. This
// directory is the second-to-last plain directory under
// lib/@vibe/compiler/ (the top-level directory itself is the true last
// one, and depends on this batch + a sibling module_graph_path.vibe
// relocation batch landing first, #897 tracking issue). Four impl files,
// no facade rename (none of them was the old index.vibe, so no
// `git mv index.vibe <dirname>.vibe` was needed):
//
//   - codegen_fingerprint.vibe: AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/generate_bundle.sh
//     (#630). A single `export let codegen_fingerprint: () -> String = ...`
//     zero-arg thunk, no imports.
//   - cache_underlying.vibe: `cache_`-prefixed forwarding wrappers around
//     the EXTERNAL @vibe/cache package's generic disk-cache primitives
//     (#769 -- real wrapper fns, not `x as cache_x` import aliases, because
//     generate_bundle.sh's bundle-merge lane resolves references by name
//     and strips relative import lines, so an alias-only rename has no
//     surviving definition). Also owns the VIBE_BUILD_CACHE_DIR override
//     (#849) via a private, non-exported `effect Env` + checker-only
//     discharge (mirrors module_graph_path.vibe's ADR-0065 pattern) so the
//     8 path-returning wrappers don't need an `Env` row on their own
//     signatures.
//   - persistent_cache.vibe: the compiler-specific adapter over
//     cache_underlying.vibe -- supplies the two identity components a
//     generic cache can't know (the codegen fingerprint, #630, and
//     VIBE_LIB's module-resolution env seed, #758) and re-exports the
//     ORIGINAL @vibe/cache wrapper names/signatures so every existing
//     compiler call site keeps working unchanged. Also owns the
//     package-index-dep staleness check (package_index_dep_is_current /
//     package_index_deps_are_current, #897) used to detect a cached
//     module-header/dep-list row naming a `@scope/name` package-index dep
//     that no longer resolves to the same on-disk root.
////   - ast_binary.vibe (#2510): the per-file binary AST format -- one
//     module's parse, encoded so a warm build can load it instead of
//     lexing and parsing the text again.
//
// `export ../../../../lib/@vibe/cache { .. }` SReExport (see
// persistent_cache.vibe's own header comment): rewritten from the old bare
// `import ../../../../lib/@vibe/cache {...}` + separate `export {...}`
// two-step, which does NOT satisfy check_contract as an implementation for
// a declared contract name (only a real local `export fn`/`export type`
// body, or an SReExport, counts) -- same fix as core/ast.vibe's identical
// rewrite for @vibe/ast's Expr/Pat/Stmt/TypeExpr. The 12 fn declarations
// below for those re-exported names are satisfied by this SReExport at
// face value; lib/@vibe/cache/index.vpkg is what actually pins their
// shape.
//
// No bare-name collision across the three files: cache_underlying.vibe's
// exports are ALL `cache_`-prefixed (cache_persistent_artifact_cache_path,
// ...) while persistent_cache.vibe's own wrappers use the un-prefixed
// `persistent_*` names -- distinct from the prelude/ batch's mid-session
// collision precedent (two files exporting the identical bare name), which
// does not recur here.
//
// No import cycle: persistent_cache.vibe's only compiler-internal
// dependency outside this directory is ../module_graph_path.vibe (a
// top-level compiler file, not yet relocated as of this batch -- see the
// tracking-issue note above), which itself only imports the external
// @vibe/core package -- it does not import cache/ back.

// --- codegen_fingerprint
fn codegen_fingerprint() -> String

